  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion:pbps-conditional-ordinary-resolvent",
    "anchor": "PBPS arXiv:2609.06905v1 Section2.2 equations2.6-2.14 actual reflected conditional law and AppendixC.1 LemmaB.1/C.1 omitted weighted-H1 analytic prerequisite. SPHMC2609.06906v1 Section4.1 BL dependency route only; the ordinary PDE is not a quoted numbered source theorem.",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
    "original_text": "Explicit analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE has the same real finite-dimensional Hilbert/Borel/full-space structure, including dimension zero. V is C2 with all-point/all-direction alpha I<=Hess V<=beta I, alpha,beta NNReal, 0<alpha<=beta; eta>0 and beta eta<=1.\nThe Gibbs/Gaussian augmentation, common Markov R/S, disintegration R, reflection S_y=(2x-y)#R_y, and true reflected W_y(u)=V((y+u)/2)+norm(u-y)^2/(8eta) are derived. Each selected S_y is precisely volume.tilted(-W_y), with positive integrable partition and C2 W_y.\nFor every y there is one original dense closable exact compact smooth gradient D_y with closed closure, fixed before epsilon and forcing. Every epsilon>0 and genuine f in L2(S_y) has one u/G serving all ordinary tests and compact sets. Existence is fiberwise; no joint measurable solution selection in y is concluded.\nFor actual source V/alpha/beta/eta, construct genuine common augmentation R/S and exact reflected conditional laws. For every y, retain the true positive integrable C2 W_y and original dense closable compact smooth gradient D_y before epsilon/input. Every epsilon>0 and actual f in L2(S_y) has u in that same closure domain, the full variational and ordinary weak-gradient identities, genuine local volume L2 of u/G/k_y, locally integrable squared norm of k_y, and for all C2 compact phi the legal ordinary volume distribution identity integral u Delta phi = integral k_y phi, where k_y=epsilon u+inner(gradient W_y,G)-f. Reflected/RGO laws and scales remain distinct.\nSame actual D/u/G and forcing yield ordinary volume distribution Delta u=epsilon u+inner(gradient W,G)-f, all C2 compact tests with genuine L1 products, and genuine local L2 of u/G/right-hand side. Full existing variational and ordinary weak-gradient identities retained. Actual PBPS R/S/reflected law and fixed fiber D before epsilon/input. No local H2, global generator core/Bochner, Poincare/BL, centered epsilon limit, noncompact constant/linear domains, measurable y-selection, SPHMC Hessian lower/full4.1 or complete paper/main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
    "text_sha256": "3fa50dfdb18870e8e80410b363630613d407166e41239d8c34fb454d6112d209"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ConditionalOrdinaryResolvent.conditional_ordinary_resolvent",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ConditionalOrdinaryResolvent.lean",
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : NNReal} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α:ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, (α:ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β:ℝ)*‖v‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β:ℝ)*η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := Measure.map (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2)) (μ.prod (stdGaussian E))\n    let W := fun y u : E => V ((1/2:ℝ) • (y+u)) + ‖u-y‖^2/(8*η)\n    ∃ R S : Kernel E E, IsMarkovKernel R ∧ IsMarkovKernel S ∧\n      (J.map Prod.swap).IsCondKernel R ∧\n      (∀ y, S y = (R y).map (fun x => (2:ℝ) • x-y)) ∧\n      ∀ y, S y = (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun u => -W y u) ∧\n        ContDiff ℝ 2 (W y) ∧ Integrable (fun u => Real.exp (-W y u)) ∧\n        0 < (∫ u, Real.exp (-W y u)) ∧\n        ∃ D : Lp ℝ 2 (S y) →ₗ.[ℝ] Lp E 2 (S y),\n          Dense (D.domain : Set (Lp ℝ 2 (S y))) ∧ D.IsClosable ∧ D.closure.IsClosed ∧\n          (∀ (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) (v : Lp E 2 (S y)), (u,v) ∈ D.graph ↔\n            ∃ f : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ ∞ f ∧ HasCompactSupport f ∧\n              u =ᵐ[S y] f ∧ v =ᵐ[S y] gradient f) ∧\n      ∀ (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε → ∀ f : Lp ℝ 2 (S y),\n      ∃ u : D.closure.domain,\n        (∀ v : D.closure.domain,\n          ε * ⟪(u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)), (v : Lp ℝ 2 (S y))⟫ +\n            ⟪D.closure u, D.closure v⟫ = ⟪f, (v : Lp ℝ 2 (S y))⟫) ∧\n        LocallyIntegrable (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x) ∧\n        LocallyIntegrable (fun x => D.closure u x) ∧\n        (∀ ψ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 1 ψ → HasCompactSupport ψ → ∀ v : E,\n          Integrable (fun x => ψ x * inner ℝ (D.closure u x) v) ∧\n          Integrable (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x * fderiv ℝ ψ x v) ∧\n          (∫ x, ψ x * inner ℝ (D.closure u x) v) =\n            - ∫ x, (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x * fderiv ℝ ψ x v) ∧\n        LocallyIntegrable (fun x => ‖ε * (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x +\n          inner ℝ (gradient (W y) x) (D.closure u x) - f x‖ ^ 2) ∧\n        (∀ K : Set E, IsCompact K →\n          MemLp (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x) 2 (volume.restrict K) ∧\n          MemLp (fun x => D.closure u x) 2 (volume.restrict K) ∧\n          MemLp (fun x => ε * (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x +\n            inner ℝ (gradient (W y) x) (D.closure u x) - f x) 2 (volume.restrict K)) ∧\n        ∀ φ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 2 φ → HasCompactSupport φ →\n          Integrable (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x * Laplacian.laplacian φ x) ∧\n          Integrable (fun x => (ε * (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x +\n            inner ℝ (gradient (W y) x) (D.closure u x) - f x) * φ x) ∧\n          (∫ x, (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x * Laplacian.laplacian φ x) =\n            ∫ x, (ε * (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x +\n              inner ℝ (gradient (W y) x) (D.closure u x) - f x) * φ x",
    "statement_sha256": "098313d6a2f3f3c8d4187e10d3f3d5d13f8090c5493bb55fcdc9cce1b6d423f6",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with Borel measurable space and canonical Lebesgue volume, including dimension zero. All section ambient instances remain part of the contract. NNReal means nonnegative real scalars.",
      "Lp F 2 mu is the true L2 quotient and its coercion selects the standard measurable representative. MemLp is actual a.e. strong measurability and finite L2 norm. All compact restrictions in the statement use volume.restrict K, and all unannotated local integrability/integrals use canonical volume.",
      "gradient is the Riesz representative of actual Frechet derivative; fderiv is total Lean derivative. Laplacian.laplacian phi is the actual test-function finite-basis trace. The theorem only tests arbitrary L2 u against this smooth-test Laplacian, and does not assert pointwise total laplacian u.",
      "LinearPMap is a real-linear partial operator on its submodule domain, with actual graph. IsClosable means its topological graph closure is single-valued. D.closure is that same closed operator. Its L2 output is the actual G representative appearing in the ordinary distribution equation.",
      "Measure.tilted h means exp(h)/integral exp(h) times the original measure; it does not build in positive normalization. Kernel IsMarkovKernel means genuine measurable probability transitions. IsCondKernel is true disintegration of the stated joint measure. Measure.map/prod mean actual pushforward/independent product. stdGaussian is the genuine standard real Hilbert Gaussian. ContDiff 1/2/infinity means C1/C2/smooth; HasCompactSupport is compact topological support."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "Focused genuine C2 compact PDE source extraction PASS; standard3 only. Independent complete mathematics/blind/source/exactcommit/shared integration pending."
  },
